-- Round 1553 (2026-10-22): Soccer Connections, every group true, one right answer a board (part A).
--
-- UNAPPLIED. Written for review; the lead applies it at a release, away from
-- midnight ET and never beside a gate on live tables. Never rehearsed on
-- production (BEGIN ... ROLLBACK still takes the locks): rehearse in PGlite
-- (scripts/qa/rehearseConnections1553.mjs does).
--
-- What it does: rewrites, IN PLACE, the connections_puzzles rows whose boards
-- this round corrected in src/data/connectionsPuzzles.ts. Same puzzle_id, same
-- sort_order, same row count, so dailyIndex deals the same board on the same
-- day and nothing reshuffles. Only groups_json changes.
--
-- Why: the dated groups said "Current ... (2025-26)" and named men who had
-- left (Sane, Son, Isak, Neymar, Insigne, Donnarumma and more); nine early
-- boards carried false claims (Rooney's treble, Drogba's Africa Cup of
-- Nations, Dani Alves's two Champions League clubs, Ramos's 90th minute
-- winner, Thiago Messi as a professional) or a second right answer, and
-- puzzle-136 said "Won the 2026 Champions League" over four Barcelona men
-- (PSG won that final) beside a Liverpool and Napoli group none of whose four
-- men played for Liverpool. Every
-- claim the new rows make stands on two hosts in
-- scripts/data/connectionsVerified2026-10/ (ledger.json and squads.json), and
-- scripts/simConnectionsFacts.mjs holds the shipped file to it.
--
-- The guard: a row is rewritten only while it still holds the exact board the
-- file held before this round (jsonb equality, so key order and spacing do not
-- matter). A row that holds anything else is left alone and named in a NOTICE,
-- never
-- overwritten blind. Six rows are known to differ already: puzzle-4, 10, 12, 75,
-- 104 and 112 as migration 20260526000004 seeded them each list one man in two
-- groups, so useConnections filters them out of the pool. If the live table
-- still holds those seeded boards they stay out: rewriting them would add
-- valid boards, change the pool size and reshuffle every daily. The pool size
-- this migration leaves is the pool size it found. Before applying, the lead exports the table once with a
-- read only SELECT (puzzle_id, sort_order, groups_json order by sort_order) and
-- runs CONN_LIVE=<export.json> node scripts/simConnectionsFacts.mjs, which
-- names every live board still carrying a refuted claim or a present tense
-- label, drifted rows included.
--
-- Saved daily guesses find a solved group by its category text
-- (src/hooks/useConnections.ts), so a board renamed on the day it is dealt
-- loses that day's solved groups on screen. Apply on a day this rewrites no
-- dealt board: node scripts/qa/connectionsDealtDay1553.mjs <export.json> <YYYY-MM-DD>
-- prints the board dealt that day and whether this migration touches it.
--
-- A re-run after a good apply is a no-op (no row still holds its old board).

